destination and its amount␀␀INPUTS␀␀OUTPUTS␀TRANSACTION ID␀␀this id changes when signed. track the FINAL one your coordinator shows. raise the fee there if it stalls.␀␀your coordinator tracks this id. an explorer sees which transaction you watch. your node does not.␀␀EASY SCAN␀␀␀no signature left this signer. your coins have not moved.␀␀␀could not write to the SD card␀␀the transaction could not be signed␀SIGN FAILED␀NETWORK FEE␀%u.%u sat/vB,  %llu.%llu%% of what you send␀files %d to %d of %d, unsigned first␀␀␀␀unsigned first, then A to Z.␀␀␀␀%d of %d files. remove some to see the rest␀UNSIGNED␀␀␀␀INPUTS: the bitcoin this transaction spends.
OUTPUTS: every place it sends bitcoin.
CHANGE: the part that comes back to you.
TXID: the tracking ID after it is sent.
FEE RATE: fee per unit of size.
LOCKTIME: the first block it can enter.
DERIVATION PATH: where your keys branch.
DESCRIPTOR: lets a coordinator watch.␀A PSBT is an unsigned transaction. Your keys never leave this signer.␀␀␀builds it, holds no keys␀␀␀␀checks it, then signs it␀␀␀␀sends it to the network␀Your coordinator builds it.␀SLIDE TO SIGN␀␀␀insert a card holding the PSBT file your coordinator saved␀␀that file is not a valid PSBT␀␀␀no .psbt files on this card␀no SD card found␀␀␀␀OPEN CAMERA␀PAID BEFORE: these keys have signed to this address already.␀␀␀␀point the camera at your coordinator␀␀␀␀could not encode the signed transaction␀it loops, hold steady␀␀␀single QR␀␀␀could not read that file (too big or unreadable)␀␀␀␀REMOVE ALL SIGNED␀␀␀these go from the card. each file needs its own hold.␀␀␀REMOVE FILES␀␀␀␀saved to the card␀␀␀scanned transaction␀the scanned data is not a valid PSBT␀␀␀␀SCAN QR␀SD card ready␀␀␀RECIPIENT GETS␀␀SIGNED ALREADY␀␀SIGNED␀␀SIGNING...␀␀SIGNING AS␀␀SIGNATURE CODE␀␀this code comes from the signature itself.

sign it again on another signer you trust.

the same code means neither changed anything.␀␀␀SIGNATURE CHECK␀you were given a %s... address. each payment to it gets its own %s... address, so this one will not match it.␀␀␀IT ASKS FOR␀WRONG KEYS: another passphrase opens other keys. unlock with the right one.

WRONG PAIRING: a coordinator was given a bare key, not a descriptor.␀␀␀these keys are on a different network. switch it in SETTINGS > SIGNER.␀␀your coordinator sent no key information. pair it again, then rebuild.␀␀SIGN␀␀␀␀TOTAL LEAVING␀␀␀DUST ATTACK: spending it links your keys to a stranger. deselect it with coin control.␀␀CHANGE OUT OF REACH: your coordinator must rescan to see it.␀␀␀␀HIGH FEE: a big slice of what you send. lower it in your coordinator.␀␀␀HIGH FEE: the fee is a big part of your inputs. lower it in your coordinator.␀␀␀INPUTS LINKED: shows %u of your addresses share one owner. use fewer coins.␀WHY FLAGGED␀TINY CHANGE: leaves a dust sized input behind. adjust the amount.␀␀␀ask your coordinator for the full previous transactions.␀␀␀␀SIGNED, STILL HERE␀␀SHOW QR␀USE A CARD␀␀CHANGE␀␀Whole coins get spent, so the rest returns.␀BACK TO YOU␀Keep a little in it and hand it over.␀␀␀HAND IT OVER␀␀␀␀Your coordinator set the rate. Higher rates go first.␀␀␀FEE RATE␀␀␀␀Where the fee comes from.␀␀␀SATS PER VBYTE␀␀THE FEE␀What you pay to get this transaction mined.␀PAID TO MINERS␀␀A short code that names your keys. Your coordinator shows the same one.␀NAMES YOUR KEYS␀It picks which keys open, real or decoy.␀␀␀␀Which keys your seed words open. Your coordinator must use the same one.␀␀␀␀DERIVATION PATH Â· BIP84␀␀␀␀WHICH KEYS OPEN␀A transaction your coordinator built for you.␀␀␀NOT SIGNED YET␀␀From coin flips, dice or the camera.␀␀␀␀NOBODY CAN GUESS␀␀␀␀Seed words that rebuild your keys. Any BIP39 compatible signer opens them.␀␀WRITE THEM DOWN␀PAIRING sends this as a QR. Nobody types it.␀␀␀␀The whole thing.␀␀␀␀It lets your coordinator see your coins. It cannot spend them.␀␀12 WORDS␀␀␀␀most seed words come in twelve␀␀24 WORDS␀␀␀␀choose it to match the seed words you have␀␀AMNESIC␀load your seed words every session␀␀NOTHING LEAVES THIS DEVICE␀␀anyone can spend these␀␀NOT A BLIND DRAW␀␀␀␀a thief tries that part␀all from one part of the list.␀␀fewer real choices␀␀some seed words came up more than once.␀cut up, mix, draw blind␀THE LIST: the same 2048 words everywhere. it is public.
YOUR DRAW: cut it up, or print BIP39 tiles, mix them in a jar and take 11 unseen.
THE LAST WORD: the device works it out. it is a checksum, not a choice.␀␀␀THE 2048 WORD LIST␀␀you cut up a word list and draw blind.␀␀one short run, typed over and over.␀any one of these completes your seed words.␀PICK THE LAST WORD␀␀your draw. the signer finds only the last word.␀every word here is the same word.␀␀␀far easier to guess␀your seed words are in list order.␀␀BLIND DRAW␀␀cut up the list, draw 11␀␀␀␀HOW IT WORKS␀␀␀␀chosen is never random␀␀THE RISK␀␀␀␀CHECK YOUR SEED WORDS␀␀␀a word is wrong or out of order.
check your paper and try again.␀␀␀␀that is not a valid set of BIP39 seed words␀DICE␀␀␀␀CAMERA AND TAPS␀NEW SEED WORDS␀␀RESTORE SEED WORDS␀␀%d of 2048 words fit yours␀␀your last word is math, not chance.␀THE BUILT IN CHECK␀␀worked out, not chosen␀␀WHAT IT IS␀␀one word copied wrong␀␀␀IT CATCHES␀␀HEADS␀␀␀you flip a coin 128 times.␀␀your seed words come only from these flips.␀FLIP A COIN␀TAILS␀␀␀heads 0 tails 1, SHA256. check on any computer.␀YOURS, NOT ITS: the randomness is your own hand, not this signer's word.
WHAT GETS REFUSED: entries that lean one way, or run in order.
NOTHING IS LOST: what you entered is kept. keep going.␀␀WHY YOU DO THIS BY HAND␀you roll a die 50 times.␀␀␀␀PATTERN␀these run in order. chance does not.␀␀␀␀your seed words come only from these rolls.␀ROLL A DIE␀␀UNDO␀␀␀␀UNEVEN␀␀some faces came up far more than the rest␀␀␀your rolls, then SHA256. check on any computer.␀a key someone can guess␀nothing lost, keep going␀␀␀␀THE FIX␀CHECK WHAT YOU ENTERED␀␀ADD YOUR TAPS␀␀␀source 1 done.␀␀the sources did not combine, so nothing was saved. you had no keys yet, so nothing was lost.␀␀␀␀NO SEED WORDS MADE␀␀good. keep it there.␀␀␀␀too dark or too plain. point somewhere busier.␀␀WHAT YOU POINT AT: the scene in front of the lens.
THE CHIP ITSELF: hardware noise, on since boot.
YOUR OWN HANDS: the exact moment of each tap.
THE TIMING INSIDE: tiny delays as this board works.
STILL NOT SURE: use DICE and check it yourself.␀␀␀␀one bad source cannot decide your keys.␀WHY FOUR SOURCES␀␀␀␀CHIP NOISE␀␀not used␀␀␀␀each code is new every time. only the seed words go on paper.␀␀␀SOURCES MIXED␀␀␀SOURCE 1   WHAT YOU POINT AT␀␀␀␀not a blank wall. gravel, leaves, a deck.␀␀␀SOURCE 2   THE CHIP ITSELF␀␀hardware noise, always running.␀SOURCE 3   YOUR OWN HANDS␀␀␀the view is frozen. move the camera.␀␀␀␀tap anywhere in here. any rhythm.␀␀␀your timing is the part no manufacturer can guess.␀␀TAP TO ADD RANDOMNESS␀␀␀saved on this device, encrypted␀WHOEVER READS THESE CAN SPEND THE COINS␀SLIDE TO SHOW␀␀␀how many seed words?␀␀␀␀saved on this device, ready every time␀␀this signer does not speak that backup's mode, or it is damaged.␀␀␀␀this signer cannot open it␀␀BACKUP NOT OPENED␀␀␀no .kef backup files on this card.␀␀insert the card that holds the .kef backup, then try again.␀pick the one to open␀␀␀␀BACKUPS ON THE CARD␀nothing is saved on this device␀a SeedQR or an encrypted backup␀an encrypted backup file␀␀␀␀LOAD YOUR SEED WORDS␀␀␀␀type the seed words from your paper.␀␀␀␀MADE WITH␀␀␀brought in from another device.␀made before this signer kept a record.␀␀NOT RECORDED␀␀␀␀HOW YOUR KEYS WERE MADE␀50 rolls or 128 flips, in one go␀␀␀␀DICE OR COIN␀␀␀␀how should the seed words be made?␀␀you aim the camera, then tap.␀␀␀12 new seed words, made on this signer␀␀this samples 3 words. the full check comes after the passphrase.␀␀␀␀3-WORD SPOT CHECK␀␀␀scan a SeedQR or an encrypted backup.

